{"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"]},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(successors:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(vertexCount:successor:)"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:steps:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/Hashable-Implementations"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": every vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has exactly one out-edge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"v → f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph (Laaksonen,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", §16.3).","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"FunctionalGraph","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph.swift#L22","fileName":"FunctionalGraph.swift"},"externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). ","type":"text"},{"code":"cycleDecomposition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"successor(of:steps:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers f^k(v) for any k.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"floydCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"brentCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which need only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states and O(1) memory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}]},{"type":"text","text":" One "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" per vertex, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":". The edge leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", so edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" vertex labels, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives a graph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g"},{"type":"text","text":" its labels back."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc: